<title>CHILE: Unimarc Chile IPO reaches 6.1 bln pesos.</title>
<headline>Unimarc Chile IPO reaches 6.1 bln pesos.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Santiago Stock Exchange's initial public offering of 44,050,000 shares in Supermercados Unimarc SA reached 6.16 billion pesos ($14.7 million) on Friday, the same day the supermarket chain placed its American Depositary Shares on Wall Street, the exchange said.</p>
<p>Bankers Trust acted as local agent in the operation. The minimum price per share was set at 140 pesos, and it opened trading at 150 pesos.</p>
<p>((-- Carlos Romero, Santiago newsroom +56-2-699-5595 x211))</p>
</text>
